# Snyk (https://snyk.io) policy file, patches or ignores known vulnerabilities.
#
# Snyk's SCM integration scans every package.json in this monorepo as a separate
# project and reads .snyk only from the directory of the manifest being scanned.
# A single root .snyk therefore does NOT cover this package, so the ignore below
# is duplicated next to each manifest that resolves deepmerge through
# @mendix/shared-charts. The full rationale lives in the root .snyk file.
#
# CVE-2026-93753: prototype-poisoning guard bypass in deepmerge <= 4.3.1.
# There is no fixed release to upgrade to; 4.3.1 is the latest published version
# and the upstream fix (TehShrike/deepmerge#274) was closed unmerged.
version: v1.25.0
ignore:
    SNYK-JS-DEEPMERGE-19964053:
        - "*":
              reason: "Not reachable: deepmerge only merges developer-authored Plotly chart config, which is already a trusted channel, so an attacker-controlled prototype on the result grants no new capability. Global Object.prototype is never modified. No fixed version exists upstream (PR #274 closed unmerged)."
